### Organization IRI ### {#organization-iri}

[=Consumers=] use the organization’s IRI to tell which datasets come from the same organization.
That only works if a publisher uses one IRI for itself across all its dataset descriptions, and if no two organizations share an IRI.
A URL of a collection website, a software supplier’s server or a web page about the organization may resolve,
but it identifies that website, server or page, not the organization.

> Therefore, the organization’s HTTP IRI *MUST* identify the organization itself.
> Publishers *SHOULD* use the same IRI in all their dataset descriptions, keep it stable over time, and make sure it resolves.

Publishers *SHOULD* use one of:

- a persistent HTTP URI, such as an [ARK](https://arks.org) or a Wikidata entity IRI (`http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1526131`);
- an IRI that the organization mints on a domain it controls, such as `https://www.example.org/id/organization`;
- the organization’s homepage (`https://www.example.org`). This is acceptable, but a homepage identifies the website as much as the organization, so prefer one of the above.

The organization’s IRI *MUST NOT* be:

- an address of the collection software or its supplier, such as a hosting server (`https://museum.hosting.supplier.example/`) or the supplier’s homepage;
- a Wikidata web page (`https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1526131`) instead of the Wikidata entity IRI;
- a URL that identifies one collection website of the organization.

The validator warns about known software supplier addresses and Wikidata web pages.
Publishers *MAY* link to other identifiers of the organization, such as its Wikidata entity, with `schema:sameAs` or `owl:sameAs`.

### ISIL identifier ### {#isil}

> Publishers *SHOULD* include the organization's [ISIL code](https://www.nationaalarchief.nl/archiveren/kennisbank/isil-codes).

<div class="example">
    An organization with an ISIL code:

    <div class="vocab-tabs">
    <pre highlight=json-ld data-vocab="schema">
        {
          "@context": "https://schema.org/",
          "@type": "Organization",
          "@id": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1526131",
          "identifier": "NL-HaKB"
        }
    </pre>
    <pre highlight=json-ld data-vocab="dcat">
        {
          "@context": {
            "dct": "http://purl.org/dc/terms/",
            "foaf": "http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/"
          },
          "@type": "foaf:Organization",
          "@id": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1526131",
          "dct:identifier": "NL-HaKB"
        }
    </pre>
    </div>
</div>

### Contact information ### {#contact}

Publishers *SHOULD* include contact information so [=consumers=] can reach them with questions or feedback.
If contact information is provided, it *MUST* include a name and e-mail address.
The e-mail address *SHOULD* be an organizational or departmental address rather than a personal one for GDPR compliance.

In Schema.org, the contact point belongs to the publisher (`schema:contactPoint`).
In DCAT-AP-NL 3.0, it belongs to the dataset or catalog (`dcat:contactPoint`),
and the e-mail address is a `mailto:` IRI.

<div class="example">
    A dataset with contact information.

    <div class="vocab-tabs">
    <pre highlight=json-ld line-numbers line-highlight="9-17" data-vocab="schema">
        {
          "@context": "https://schema.org/",
          "@type": "Dataset",
          "publisher": {
            "@type": "Organization",
            "@id": "http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1526131",
            "name": "Koninklijke Bibliotheek",
            "alternateName": "KB",
            "contactPoint": {
              "@type": "ContactPoint",
              "name": {
                "@value": "Datasets Department",
                "@language": "en"
              },
              "email": "datasets@kb.nl",
              "telephone": "+31 6 12345678"
            }
          }
        }
    </pre>
    <pre highlight=json-ld line-numbers line-highlight="7-16" data-vocab="dcat">
        {
          "@context": {
            "dcat": "http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#",
            "vcard": "http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#"
          },
          "@type": "dcat:Dataset",
          "dcat:contactPoint": {
            "@type": "vcard:Kind",
            "vcard:fn": {
              "@value": "Datasets Department",
              "@language": "en"
            },
            "vcard:hasEmail": {
              "@id": "mailto:datasets@kb.nl"
            }
          }
        }
    </pre>
    </div>
</div>

### Dataset publisher ### {#dataset-publisher}

The person/organization data is then included as the dataset's publisher:

